  "selection": "Three carriers and two laws. The carriers are the triangle, the three-edge chain, and the four-cycle. The laws are the empty list and one multiply by 3 of edge (0,1) when edge (1,2) is present. Baseline cells are the canonical line graph and the carrier orbit. Constrained cells add the position-indexed line graph. The baseline position-indexed map is the atlas-008 cell and is not repeated. Cover observations are not cells. Not scheduled to explain the atlas-008 defects, the atlas-009 marginals, PAT-010, PAT-011, PAT-012, EQ-020, EQ-022, or EQ-023. A difference between carriers is joint with the placement of the designated pair on that carrier.",
